 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nMetadataEndpoint initialization broken - claims not properly set\n\n#### Description\n\nThe MetadataEndpoint constructor is not properly initializing the claims. When creating a MetadataEndpoint with initial claims, the claims are not being set correctly, causing the metadata response to be empty or incorrect.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.endpoints.metadata import MetadataEndpoint\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.endpoints.token import TokenEndpoint\n\n# Create a simple metadata endpoint with basic claims\nendpoint = TokenEndpoint(None, None, grant_types={'password': None})\nmetadata = MetadataEndpoint([endpoint], {'issuer': 'https://foo.bar', 'token_endpoint': 'https://foo.bar/token'})\n\n# Check if claims are properly set\nprint(\"Claims:\", metadata.claims)\nprint(\"Initial claims:\", metadata.initial_claims)\n\n# Try to create a metadata response\nheaders, body, status = metadata.create_metadata_response('/', 'GET')\nprint(\"Response body:\", body)\n```\n\nExpected: The claims should contain the issuer and other metadata fields.\nActual: The claims are empty or missing expected values.\n</issue>\n",
